From 03e737caf95005d5d97467df777ded49a5be1992 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Gotwalt <gotwalt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:53:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(iroh): add Builder::stateless_reset_key

An endpoint that stops without closing its connections (crash, killed
process, evicted host) leaves its peers waiting for their idle timeout.
QUIC stateless resets exist to shorten that, but they cannot work across
a restart today: iroh generates a random reset key and noq a random
HashedConnectionIdGenerator key on every bind. The new instance therefore
classifies every old connection ID as invalid and drops the packet
(noq-proto endpoint.rs: CID validation runs before stateless_reset), and
even if it did answer, the token would not match.

Builder::stateless_reset_key([u8; 32]) supplies one secret from which
both the noq reset key and the CID generator key are derived (blake3
derive_key, distinct contexts), so they cannot get out of sync. Without
it, behaviour is unchanged: a fresh random key per bind and noq's default
CID generator.

No noq changes are needed: EndpointConfig::reset_key, ::cid_generator and
HashedConnectionIdGenerator::from_key are public in noq-proto 1.4.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
